    "claim": "Sensitivity to seven named instruction contracts on one fictional 50-adult roster and four fixed model configurations. Not representative language, national-population or LLM-family effects.",
    "missingness": "Never zero-fill failures or undefined endpoints. A schedule block is complete for a contrast only when all four models have a defined endpoint in both arms. With all eight blocks complete, inference is unchanged from analysis v1. Otherwise incomplete blocks are dropped from that contrast only and inference uses the remaining blocks if at least six remain; with fewer, primary inference is suppressed and the hypothesis keeps its place in the family. Dropping a block assumes its missingness is unrelated to the contrast outcome given schedule and condition. Every result reports excluded blocks, missing cells, [0, 1]-bounded missing-data extremes over all eight blocks, and terminal failure/undefined-endpoint counts by method, condition and model as sensitivity evidence. Without a terminal receipt, execution status is unknown, not unattempted. Fallback results are labelled PARTIAL, never COMPLETE. No stopping based on interim p-values.",
    "inference": "Paired schedule-block t diagnostics on the complete blocks of each contrast (n-1 degrees of freedom for n complete blocks), Holm across exactly 24 hypotheses, Bonferroni simultaneous intervals. Assumes independent blocks and an adequate approximation for their mean. No equivalence or guaranteed power claim.",
    "secondary": "All categorical Coleman indices, age assortativity, modularity, degree distribution, per-model contrasts and matched controls remain descriptive. Do not select a primary from the strongest calibration result.",
