  "execution_order": "Schedule-block-major: seeds 44000-44007 in ascending order; the 112 cells of each block are shuffled by one Random(execution_order_seed) consumed block by block. A stop leaves complete earlier blocks. Pairing removes shared additive block effects, not arbitrary provider drift or model-by-condition changes within a block.",
  "global_parser": "Validate every line; collapse exact undirected duplicates; retain raw response and flags; NONE valid.",
  "transport_policy": "SDK retries zero. Stop on uncertain transport; retain full reservation. `recover` (or launch --auto-recover) retires one lost-transport attempt with no saved reply and permits one replacement of that same request; 4xx, received replies, a failed replacement or more than 30 retirements stop for human review. Interrupted retirement journals/logs are reconciled from the unchanged ledger before any new request.",
  "max_transport_recoveries": 30,
  "replacements_per_request": 1,
  "local_write_policy": "Atomic JSON writes retry PermissionError only, at most ten times after the initial attempt (0.05, 0.1, 0.25, 0.5, 1, 2, 5, 10, 15, 20 seconds; about 54 s). Retry identical local data, never transport or parsing. Exhaustion stops for inspection.",
  "journal_reconciliation_policy": "`recover` (or launch --auto-recover) may rewrite one stale request journal from the unchanged ledger only when the row is received, its transport receipt matches, and the journal equals the intent record or the exact pre-parse row digest. Each repair is logged; at most 30 per run. Existing log provenance is validated against received rows before further recovery or requests. Any other mismatch stops for human review.",
  "max_journal_reconciliations": 30,
  "scheduler_policy": "Optional walltime pauses only between requests, before intent creation, using one monotonic deadline across recovery loops. Received replies and partial cells resume under the identical authorization and ledger. PAUSED_AT_CHECKPOINT exits 75; other failures never trigger scheduler resubmission. No concurrent collectors.",
  "partial_analysis": "`analyze --stage main` replays every saved receipt offline and reports a stopped or failed inventory under the predeclared analysis fallback, labelled PARTIAL.",
